From 0a297a8c7cd1ffcde43070dd0f5058900eaad9d9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Lukschander <oliver.lukschander@golf.at>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 09:12:03 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] thunderbolt: apple: dump the ACIO analog block on every
 DP-aux poll

Pure diagnostic, no behavior change: apple_dp_aux_work() already reads
the DP IN adapter's CS0-13 registers every 500ms for up to 12s, but only
dumped the deeper ACIO analog block (the actual AUX/DPCD serializer,
"dpin0/1 analog") once, at the very end. Every host-side register fix
tried so far (0129 set_hpd timeout, 0130 linkcfg timeout, 0131 HPD
propagate, 0132 NO_AUTO_LT + video credits) leaves DCP's own ~5-second
internal wait before DEVICE_NOT_RESPONDING/DEVICE_NOT_STARTED completely
unchanged, and the analog block's own internal FSM state (offset +0x18)
has never actually been observed moment-to-moment during that window --
only a single post-mortem snapshot after the full 12s poll budget was
already spent. This makes the dump unconditional on every poll instead,
so the next capture shows whether that FSM (or anything else in the
block) ever moves during DCP's own attempt, or stays static throughout --
a genuinely new, currently-missing piece of evidence rather than another
guess at a register to poke. Full reasoning in notes/2026-09-24-0133-*.md.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/thunderbolt/apple.c | 18 ++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/thunderbolt/apple.c b/drivers/thunderbolt/apple.c
index d18ecb8..db25b75 100644
--- a/drivers/thunderbolt/apple.c
+++ b/drivers/thunderbolt/apple.c
@@ -1039,13 +1039,23 @@ static void apple_dp_aux_work(struct work_struct *work)
 		tb_port_warn(port, "DP IN DPRX_DONE=1 (ACIO AUX completed)\n");
 
 	anhi->dp_aux_polls++;
+	/*
+	 * Diagnostic (candidate 0133, see notes/2026-09-24-0133-*.md): dump
+	 * the analog block on every poll, not just the last one. Every
+	 * host-side register fix so far (0129-0132) leaves DCP's own
+	 * ~5-second internal wait before DEVICE_NOT_RESPONDING unchanged, so
+	 * the open question is what (if anything) the ACIO analog block
+	 * itself is doing during that window -- not yet observed, since the
+	 * only prior dump was a single snapshot after the whole 12s poll
+	 * budget was already spent.
+	 */
+	if (anhi->acio)
+		apple_dp_dump_analog(anhi->acio,
+				     dprx ? "dpin0 analog DPRX done" :
+					    "dpin0 analog poll");
 	if (!dprx && anhi->dp_aux_polls < APPLE_DP_AUX_POLL_MAX) {
 		mod_delayed_work(system_wq, &anhi->dp_aux_work,
 				 msecs_to_jiffies(APPLE_DP_AUX_POLL_MS));
-	} else if (anhi->acio) {
-		apple_dp_dump_analog(anhi->acio,
-				     dprx ? "dpin0 analog DPRX done" :
-					    "dpin0 analog at timeout");
 	}
 
 out_unlock:
